    historyContent: {
      origins: 'Tute originated in Italy as tutti and spread to Spain in the 19th century, becoming one of the most popular card games there. Tute cabrero is an individual-play variant for 3 to 6 players, popular in Argentina and Uruguay. It uses the same 40-card Spanish deck and marriage-style point-trick structure as partnership Tute but with elimination (four losses) and a first-hand rule that coins are trumps and the holder of the two of coins leads. The variant is described in Spanish card-game literature and on dedicated Tute Cabrero pages.',
